This project has a graphify knowledge graph at graphify-out/. **`graphify-out/` is
gitignored — it is a per-clone, local-only cache, never committed.** It must be
bootstrapped once after cloning/pulling and kept fresh while you work; it is not
something you can rely on already existing.

**Bootstrap first (only when missing):** if `graphify-out/graph.json` does not
exist yet — fresh clone, or `graphify-out/` was deleted — run `just graphify-init`
(wraps `graphify extract . --code-only`, no API key needed) before doing anything
else. Do this once, up front; do not start exploring with raw Read/Grep/Glob
instead just because the graph is momentarily missing. If `just` is unavailable,
run the underlying `graphify extract . --code-only` directly, or invoke the full
`/graphify` skill for a richer build that also covers docs.

Once a graph exists, run `just graphify-hooks` (wraps `graphify hook install`) if
you have not already — it installs local post-commit/post-checkout git hooks
(`.git/hooks`, not versioned, so this is per-clone) that keep the graph
auto-refreshed as code changes and branches switch, on top of the manual
`graphify update .` step below.

**MANDATORY: Before using Read, Grep, Glob, or Bash to explore the codebase, you MUST run graphify first:**
- `graphify query "<question>"` — scoped subgraph for any codebase or architecture question
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — dependency path between two symbols
- `graphify explain "<concept>"` — all nodes related to a concept

This applies to YOU and to every subagent you spawn. Include this rule explicitly in every subagent prompt that involves code exploration. Do not skip graphify because files are "already known" or because you are executing a plan — the graph surfaces cross-file dependencies and INFERRED edges that grep and Read cannot find.

Only use Read/Grep/Glob directly when:
1. graphify has already oriented you and you need to modify or debug specific lines
2. bootstrapping the graph itself is not possible in the current environment (no `graphify` binary, no network) — state that explicitly rather than silently skipping it

- If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, navigate it instead of reading raw files
- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for broad architecture review when query/path/explain do not surface enough context
- After modifying code files, run `graphify update .` to keep the graph current (AST-only, no API cost)
